==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|testimonial|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{term|testimonialis||of or pertaining to testimony}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|testimonium||testimony|lang=la}}; see [[testimony]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[statement]], especially one given under [[oath]]; [[testimony]]
# A written [[recommendation]] of someone's [[worth]] or [[character]]
# A [[tribute]] given in [[appreciation]] of someone's [[service]] etc.
# {{context|football}} A [[match]] played in tribute to a particular player (who sometimes receives a proportion of the gate money).

====Related terms====
* [[testify]]
* [[testimony]]

